# Meta WhatsApp Integration Rules

This service uses Meta WhatsApp Cloud API as the official messaging provider.

## Integration principles

- Treat Meta as an infrastructure provider.
- Isolate Meta-specific code inside the whatsapp/infrastructure layer.
- Never spread Graph API request details across the codebase.
- All outgoing WhatsApp calls should go through a dedicated provider/client.

## Required integration boundaries

Create a dedicated client/provider for:
- webhook verification
- parsing inbound webhook payloads
- sending text/template messages
- mapping Meta responses into internal DTOs

## Webhook rules

Expose:
- GET /webhook for verification
- POST /webhook for inbound events

Webhook handlers must:
- validate payload structure
- ignore unsupported event types safely
- normalize inbound messages into internal shapes
- delegate processing to use cases

## Message sending rules

All outgoing messages must:
- go through a single client abstraction
- return a typed result
- include provider response IDs when available
- log success and failure clearly

## Template/session mindset

Design the provider in a way that supports:
- template messages
- free-form/session messages

Do not hardcode the codebase around a single message type forever.

## Error handling

Meta API errors must be:
- captured
- logged with enough context
- mapped to typed application errors when appropriate

Avoid silent failures.

## Direct WhatsApp links

When the seeker should contact the responder directly, generate a wa.me link using a dedicated utility/use case.
Do not generate raw links ad hoc in controllers or string templates scattered across files.

## Tone and messaging

Outgoing WhatsApp messages should be:
- brief
- human
- direct
- clear
- operational

Avoid robotic language and avoid long multi-paragraph messages.